        "original_id": "633144fc-b4e6-5014-8a5d-9c61db6be2e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Raimond Aumann, Baloo, Sven Scheuer, Oliver Kahn, Rudyard Kipling\n- Organizations: Bayern Munich\n- Works: The Jungle Book, The Second Jungle Book\n- Concepts: Nicknames, fictional characters, goalkeepers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1894, Rudyard Kipling featured Baloo as a main fictional character in The Jungle Book.\n- In 1895, Rudyard Kipling featured Baloo as a main fictional character in The Second Jungle Book.\n- Baloo means \"bear\" and comes from the Hindi word \"Bhālū.\"\n- In 1988, Sven Scheuer joined Bayern Munich.\n- Sven Scheuer spent 11 years with Bayern Munich.\n- Until 1994, Sven Scheuer served as backup goalkeeper to Raimond Aumann at Bayern Munich.\n- After 1994, Sven Scheuer served as backup goalkeeper to Oliver Kahn at Bayern Munich.\n- Raimond Aumann's nickname is Balu, a Germanized version of Baloo from The Jungle Book.",
